{"name":"Japanese Cypress","hex":"#965036","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cypress","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen coniferous tree with flattened shoots bearing small scale-like leaves, whose dark foliage is sometimes associated with mourning, in family Cupressaceae, especially the genera Cupressus and Chamaecyparis."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Cyprus (“type of fabric”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cypress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chamaecyparis obtusa","blocks":[{"text":"Chamaecyparis obtusa is a species of conifer in the cypress family, Cupressaceae native to central Japan in East Asia, and widely cultivated in the temperate northern hemisphere for its high-quality timber and ornamental qualities, with many cultivars commercially available.\nIt once existed outside Asia with a range that stretched to Germany during the Miocene. Hinoki grows primarily on the islands of Honshu, Shikoku, and Kyushu. The main massifs are formed in mountainous regions with a moderately humid climate, at altitudes from 300 to 1,500 meters above sea level."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/%E5%A4%A7%E6%99%BA%E5%AF%BA_%28%E5%B2%90%E9%98%9C%E5%B8%82%29-%E6%A8%B9%E9%BD%A2%E7%B4%84700%E5%B9%B4%E3%81%AE%E5%A4%A7%E3%83%92%E3%83%8E%E3%82%ADdaichiji008.jpg/330px-%E5%A4%A7%E6%99%BA%E5%AF%BA_%28%E5%B2%90%E9%98%9C%E5%B8%82%29-%E6%A8%B9%E9%BD%A2%E7%B4%84700%E5%B9%B4%E3%81%AE%E5%A4%A7%E3%83%92%E3%83%8E%E3%82%ADdaichiji008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamaecyparis_obtusa","wikidata":"Q917187"},{"title":"Cypress","blocks":[{"text":"Cypress is a common name for species in several genera in the family Cupressaceae. They grow in temperate climates and subtropical regions of Asia, Europe, and North America."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cypress","wikidata":"Q14169641"}],"images":[{"